          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphism"} formally étale morphism
            between
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p We first state the traditional
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#ExplicitlyInComponents"} Explicit definition in components
          %p Then we give the abstract
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#CharacterizationByReductionModality"} Characterization by reduction/infinitesimal shape/de Rham Space
          %h3#ExplicitlyInComponents Explicitly in components
          #ExplicitDefinition.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \hookrightarrow A
              is called
              %em formally étale
              if for every ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              and for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+ideal"} nilpotent ideal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subset B
              and for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    B/I &amp;\leftarrow&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\leftarrow&amp; R
                    }
            %p there is a unique diagonal morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    B/I &amp;\leftarrow&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow &amp;\swarrow&amp; \uparrow
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\leftarrow&amp; R
                    }
            %p that makes both triangles commute.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#StackProject"} Stacks Project 57.9, 57.12
          %p
            By
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} formal duality
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} locality
            this yields a notion of formally étale morphisms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+varieties"} affine varieties
            and of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
          %h3#CharacterizationByReductionModality Characterization by reduction/infinitesimal shape
          #ReductionOnRings.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing_{fin}
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+ring"} finitely generated
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
              and write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                      %mi ext
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing_{fin}^{ext}
              for the category of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+ring+extensions"} infinitesimal ring extensions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Red
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                      %mi ext
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Red \;\colon\; CRing_{fin}^{ext} \longrightarrow CRing_{fin}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              which sends an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+ring+extension"} infinitesimal ring extension
              to the underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              (in the maximal case this sends a commutative ring to its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+ring"} reduced ring
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                    %mo ↪
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                      %mi ext
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i \;\colon\; CRing_{fin} \hookrightarrow CRing_{fin}^{ext}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              inclusion that regards a ring as the trivial infinitesimal extension over itself.
          #DifferentialCohesionModality.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              There is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"}> co
              \-)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Red
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi inf
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi inf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                      %mi ext
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                      %mi ext
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (Red \dashv \int_{inf} \dashv \flat_{inf}) \;\colon\; PSh((CRing_{fin}^{ext})^{op}) \longrightarrow PSh((CRing_{fin}^{ext})^{op})
            %p
              where the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Red
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Red
              is given on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representables
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+scheme"} reduction
              functor of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReductionOnRings"}
              (followed by the inclusion).
          %p
            This statement and the following prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalEtalenessBydeRhamSpace"}
            is a slight paraphrase of an observation due to (
            %a{:href => "Q-category#KontsevichRosenbergSpaces"}> Kontsevich-Rosenberg 04
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The functors from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReductionOnRings"}
              form an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+pair"} adjoint pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Red
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Red \dashv i)
              because an extension element can only map to an extension element; so for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi R
                      %mo ^
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat R \to R
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+ring+extension"} infinitesimal ring extension
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo =
                      %mi Red
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi R
                        %mo ^
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = Red(\widehat R)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              a commutative ring with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i(S) = (S \to S)
              its trivial extension, there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi CRing
                          %mi fin
                          %mi ext
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi R
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi CRing
                          %mi fin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{CRing_{fin}^{ext}}(\widehat R, i(S))
                    \\simeq
                    Hom_{CRing_{fin}}(R,S)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing_{fin}
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi CRing
                        %mi fin
                        %mi ext
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing_{fin}^{ext}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Red
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi i
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi Red
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                      %mi ext
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (Red \dashv i)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    CRing_{fin}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{Red}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{i}{\hookrightarrow}}
                    CRing_{fin}^{ext}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Via
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
              this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+pair"} adjoint pair
              induces an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+presheaves"} categories of presheaves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mover
                          %munder
                            %mo ←
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi Red
                                %mo *
                          %mover
                            %mo ↪
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi Red
                                %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi Red
                              %mo !
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mo !
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                      %mi ext
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    PSh(CRing_{fin}^{op})
                    \\stackrel{\overset{i_!}{\hookrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{i^\ast = Red_!}{\leftarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{Red^\ast}{\hookrightarrow}}{\underset{Red_\ast}{\leftarrow}}}}
                    PSh((CRing_{fin}^{ext})^{op})
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
              to be shown is obtained from composing these adjoints pairwise.
            %p
              That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Red
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Red
              coincides with the reduction functor on representables is a standard property of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Kan+extension"} left Kan extension
              (see
              %a{:href => "Kan+extension#LeftKanOnRepresentables"} here
              for details).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              These considerations make sense in the general abstract context of “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"}> differential cohesion
              ” where the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
              of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialCohesionModality"}
              would be called:
            %p
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+modality"} reduction modality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊣
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊣
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+flat+modality"} infinitesimal flat modality
          %p
            Due to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!
            in the proof of prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialCohesionModality"}
            we may equivalently regard presheaves on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi CRing
                    %mi fin
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (CRing_{fin})^{op}
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi CRing
                    %mi fin
                    %mi ext
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (CRing_{fin}^{ext})^{op}
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+schemes"} formal schemes
          #FormalEtalenessBydeRhamSpace.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \;\colon\; Spec A \to Spec R
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                      %mi op
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing_{fin}^{op} \hookrightarrow PSh(CRing_{fin}^{op})
              is formally étale, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExplicitDefinition"}
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi inf
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_{inf}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type"} modal
              relative
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality square
              of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Spec
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ∫
                              %mi inf
                            %mi Spec
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Spec
                            %mi R
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ∫
                              %mi inf
                            %mi Spec
                            %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Spec A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \int_{inf} Spec A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    Spec R &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \int_{inf} Spec R
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              square.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Evaluated on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi fin
                      %mi ext
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \hookrightarrow R  \to R/I \in CRing_{fin}^{ext}
              any object, by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              and the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Red
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi inf
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Red \dashv \int_{inf})
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              the naturality square becomes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi CRing
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi CRing
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi I
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi CRing
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi R
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi CRing
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi R
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi I
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    CRing(A,B) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; CRing(A,B/I)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    CRing(R,B) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; CRing(R,B/I)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              precisely if the condition in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExplicitDefinition"}
              holds.
          %p
            The basic stability property of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphisms"} étale morphisms
          #ClosureForFormallyEtale.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \stackrel{f}{\to} \stackrel{g}{\to}
              two composable morphisms, then
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                  are both (formally) étale, then so is their composite
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi g
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \circ f
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\circ f
                  are (formally) étale, then so is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                  of a (formally) étale morphism along any morphism is again (formally) étale.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              With prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalEtalenessBydeRhamSpace"}
              this is equivalently the statement of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              diagrams.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_tale_morphism Relation to étale morphism
          %p
            Formally étale morphisms of schemes which are in addition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+of+finite+presentation"} locally of finite presentation
            are equivalently
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphisms+of+schemes"} étale morphisms of schemes
          %p
            Relaxing this finiteness condition yields the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+%C3%A9tale+morphisms"} weakly étale morphisms
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphism+of+schemes"} étale morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⇒
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-%C3%A9tale+morphism+of+schemes"} pro-étale morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⇒
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+%C3%A9tale+morphism+of+schemes"} weakly étale morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⇒
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphism+of+schemes"} formally étale morphism
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+unramified+morphism"}> formally unramified morphism
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+smooth+morphisms"} formally smooth morphisms
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basics+of+%C3%A9tale+cohomology"} basics of étale cohomology
          %h2#references References
          %p The traditional formulation is for instance in
          %ul#StackProject
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Stacks+Project"}> The Stacks Project
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04G3"} 57.9. Formally smooth, étale, unramified transformations
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04GB"} 57.12. Formally étale morphisms
          %p
            The characterization via a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+modality"} reduction modality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊣
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
          %ul#SimpsonTeleman97
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Simpson"}> Carlos Simpson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em
                de Rham Theorem for
                = succeed "-stacks" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              1997 (
              %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~teleman/math/simpson.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %ul#KontsevichRosenberg04
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"} Alexander Rosenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em Noncommutative spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/KontsevichRosenbergNCSpaces.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preprints/send?bid=2331"} ps
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preprints/send?bid=2303"} dvi
          %p
            The formalization as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              , sections 3.5, 3.10 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.7930"}> arXiv:1310.7930
              )
